 "intro": "Future time clauses take the subjunctive; «antes de que» always does. With the same subject, «antes de» and «después de» take the infinitive.",
 "palabras": [
  {
   "palabra": "antes de que",
   "significado": "before (someone does)",
   "pron": "AN-tes de ke",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It always takes the subjunctive: the action has not happened yet. «Llámame antes de que salgas».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "después de que",
   "significado": "after (someone does)",
   "pron": "des-PWES de ke",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "If it is future, subjunctive; if it already happened, indicative: «después de que cenemos» or «después de que cenamos».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "hasta que",
   "significado": "until",
   "pron": "AS-ta ke",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "Pending future: subjunctive («hasta que llegues»). Past or habit: indicative («hasta que llegó»).",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "tan pronto como",
   "significado": "as soon as",
   "pron": "tan PRON-to KO-mo",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It means the same as «en cuanto». With a pending future it takes the subjunctive.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "mientras",
   "significado": "while",
   "pron": "MYEN-tras",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "conjunction",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "With the indicative it describes two things at once: «mientras cocino, escucho música».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "antes de",
   "significado": "before (doing)",
   "pron": "AN-tes de",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "preposition",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It goes with the infinitive if the subject does not change: «antes de salir, apago la luz».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "después de",
   "significado": "after (doing)",
   "pron": "des-PWES de",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "preposition",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "Also with the infinitive: «después de cenar, leo». The final d sounds soft.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "avísame",
   "significado": "let me know",
